   "evidence": "Exclusive/Kinematics/Basic.lean:59-60 `def Q2 (g : Bilin V) (K : ExclKinematics V) : \u211d := - g K.q K.q`; Kinematics/Basic.lean:71-72 `def Q2 ... := - g K.q K.q`. Contrast the sibling `tMom_toExclKinematics` (line 192), which does route through `delta_toExclKinematics` rather than `rfl`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Diffractive/Kinematics/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Prove it through the existing projection lemma: `rw [ExclKinematics.Q2, DisKinematics.Q2, toExclKinematics_q]` (or `simp only [...]`), so the proof states why the two scales agree instead of relying on exposed bodies matching.",
   "issue": "`Q2_toExclKinematics` is proved by `(rfl)`, which holds only because `ExclKinematics.Q2` and `DisKinematics.Q2` happen to have identical bodies (`- g K.q K.q`); the defeq spans two unrelated definitions in different namespaces and is undocumented.",
